(c) Estimate the percentage who scored below $69$.
(d) Estimate how many scored below $69$.

workedExamples.solution_text:
The box edges give $Q_1=33$ and $Q_3=69$; the line inside gives the median, $51$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (1.7,0.4)--(3.3,0.4);
\draw[thick] (6.9,0.4)--(8.6,0.4);
\draw[thick] (1.7,0.2)--(1.7,0.6);
\draw[thick] (8.6,0.2)--(8.6,0.6);
\draw[thick,fill=none] (3.3,0) rectangle (6.9,0.8);
\draw[thick] (5.1,0)--(5.1,0.8);
\node[above] at (1.7,0.9) {$17$};
\node[above] at (3.3,0.9) {$Q_1=33$};
\node[above] at (5.1,0.9) {Median $51$};
\node[above] at (6.9,0.9) {$Q_3=69$};
\node[above] at (8.6,0.9) {$86$};
\node[below] at (2.5,-0.15) {$25\%$};
\node[below] at (4.2,-0.15) {$25\%$};
\node[below] at (6,-0.15) {$25\%$};
\node[below] at (7.75,-0.15) {$25\%$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) The middle $50\%$ lies in the box, between **$33$ and $69$**.

(b) Above $Q_3$ is one quarter: **about $25\%$**.

(c) Below $Q_3$ are three quarters: $3\times25\%=75\%$, so **about $75\%$**.

(d) Estimated number:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}0.75\times156\\&=117\end{aligned}$

About **$117$ students**.

workedExamples.question_text:
The box plot summarises the lengths of $120$ babies born at a hospital.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (-0.3,0)--(6.4,0);
\foreach \x/\v in {0/32,1/37,2/42,3/47,4/52,5/57,6/62}{\draw (\x,-0.08)--(\x,0.08);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.12) {$\v$};}
\node[below] at (3,-0.6) {Length (cm)};
\draw[thick] (0,1.1)--(2,1.1);
\draw[thick] (4,1.1)--(6,1.1);
\draw[thick] (0,0.9)--(0,1.3);
\draw[thick] (6,0.9)--(6,1.3);
\draw[thick,fill=none] (2,0.7) rectangle (4,1.5);
\draw[thick] (3,0.7)--(3,1.5);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Between which lengths does the lowest $50\%$ lie?
(b) Below which length does approximately $75\%$ lie?
(c) Above which length does approximately $25\%$ lie?
(d) Estimate the percentage with lengths between $42$ cm and $52$ cm.
(e) Estimate how many babies are shorter than $42$ cm.
(f) Estimate how many babies have lengths between $47$ cm and $52$ cm.
(g) Estimate how many babies have lengths between $42$ cm and $52$ cm.

workedExamples.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0.4)--(2,0.4);
\draw[thick] (4,0.4)--(6,0.4);
\draw[thick] (0,0.2)--(0,0.6);
\draw[thick] (6,0.2)--(6,0.6);
\draw[thick,fill=none] (2,0) rectangle (4,0.8);
\draw[thick] (3,0)--(3,0.8);
\node[above] at (0,0.9) {$32$};
\node[above] at (2,0.9) {$42$};
\node[above] at (3,0.9) {$47$};
\node[above] at (4,0.9) {$52$};
\node[above] at (6,0.9) {$62$};
\node[below] at (1,-0.15) {$25\%$};
\node[below] at (2.5,-0.15) {$25\%$};
\node[below] at (3.5,-0.15) {$25\%$};
\node[below] at (5,-0.15) {$25\%$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The minimum is $32$ cm, $Q_1=42$ cm, the median is $47$ cm and $Q_3=52$ cm.

(a) The lowest half runs from the minimum to the median: **$32$ cm to $47$ cm**.

(b) Three quarters lie below $Q_3$: **$52$ cm**.

(c) The upper quarter lies above $Q_3$: **$52$ cm**.

(d) The whole box contains two quarters: **about $50\%$**.

(e) Below $Q_1$ is one quarter.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}0.25\times120\\&=30\end{aligned}$

About **$30$ babies**.

(f) Between the median and $Q_3$ is one quarter.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}0.25\times120\\&=30\end{aligned}$

About **$30$ babies**.

(g) Between $Q_1$ and $Q_3$ is half the dataset.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}0.5\times120\\&=60\end{aligned}$

About **$60$ babies**.

